#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`ig-cache.sh restore --ig-root .` fetches `cat/fhir-harness/fhir-ast/<package id>` into `output-ast/` (with the Publisher's `txcache/`), then `ig-cache.sh verify` runs `ig-ast.ts validity`: exit 0 valid, 1 stale-inputs (naming which input), 2 cannot-tell. A restore that finds no branch is a miss, judged as not valid. In an IG repository's site route this is the first `pre` step, `ig-site:ast` (`ig-repo-site.ts ast`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:114
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`ig-cache.sh seed --ig-root . --push`: one commit holding the AST, the Publisher's expansions and `txcache/`, the IG API generated over that AST (`ig-api/`, `ig-api-cache.ts`) and the artefact index built from that tree (`fhir-artifact-index/index.json`, `ig-index-cache.ts`), which the site reads by raw URL; its subject recording the package, counts, Publisher version and source commit. Refused when the candidate is under 90% of the incumbent's resources or edges (the no-shrink gate)."
msgstr ""

