#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How an IG repository's own site is published, and how the AST it is built from is kept current (skill `ig-build-pipeline` §\"The AST cache lifecycle\"). THE RULE. An IG site is built from the IG Publisher AST read from the IG repository's cache branch `cat/fhir-harness/fhir-ast/<package id>`, never from Publisher HTML. The publish refuses an AST that is not valid for the commit it publishes (`ig-cache.sh restore` then `verify`). A later commit that changes no IG input (`sushi-config.yaml`, `ig.ini`, `input/`) does not make the AST stale. THE REFRESH. The cache is written by ONE thing: fhir-harness's reusable workflow `.github/workflows/ig-ast-refresh.yml`, which an IG repository's Site publish calls as its first job (`ast`; template `templates/ig-repo-site/site-publish.yml`). It runs the Publisher through the AST exporter on a GitHub runner (Java, 10 GB heap, tx.fhir.org). It seeds the branch only from a commit on the default branch whose inputs equal the tip's. A valid AST is a cache, not a release: every page drawn from it carries the provisional mark (`ig-ast-delta`)."
msgstr ""

