#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the site route's steps via `stage-local.ts` → `build-instance-site.ts`: `ig-site:sidecars` (IG API sidecars, if the landing layer has the step), `ig-site:compose` (artefact index and thin pages from the AST, the IG composed at the root), `ig-site:openapi` (if the IG holds OpenAPI pages), `ig-site:publisher-pages` (the AST's resources as `<Type>-<id>.json` at the root, the build stamp), and last `ig-site:bar` (the IG's slim bar on pages written after `publisher-pages`). Published at the root from the default branch, as a preview otherwise. When the restore recorded the cache commit, the site reads the AST from that commit by raw URL rather than copying it: the artefact pages draw each full resource there, the IG API sidecars are read from its `ig-api/` (fhir-harness#344), and the artefact index from its `fhir-artifact-index/index.json`, which the site points at with `fhir-artifact-index/index.ref.json` instead of serving (#358). The root `<Type>-<id>.json` copies are then reduced (minified, no narrative, no ELM data; #359), and the JSON-LD graph (`artifact/*.jsonld`) names each root file first and the cache copy as its mirror. The full resources are the cache commit's and the release's `package.tgz`."
msgstr ""

